{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pulls/702","id":4860855805,"node_id":"PR_kwDOQugs888AAAABIbrF_Q","html_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/702","diff_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/702.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/702.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/issues/702","number":702,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Keep TCP request deadlines from closing shared connections","user":{"login":"codexcoder21","id":216437543,"node_id":"U_kgDODOaTJw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216437543?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21","html_url":"https://github.com/codexcoder21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"TinySite publishing and CI uploads lose shared backend RPC connections when one forwarded call reaches its 30-second deadline. The owner asked to preserve sibling requests and uncertain operation outcomes, with the matching ContainerNursery work in https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/ContainerNursery/pull/656. Final review also found that a connected peer which never answers could retain abandoned request IDs indefinitely, so this change bounds that state and defines when silence retires the connection.\n\nThe TCP contract is:\n\n| Invariant | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Individual expiry | A response deadline or interruption while waiting for a reply settles only that caller. A 40-second cold start can still serve siblings and later calls. |\n| Bounded reservations | Refuse admission before writing at 64 abandoned unanswered IDs or 256 total outstanding correlations. The total bound matches the existing default server handler limit and preserves the existing 65-or-more live-caller contract. |\n| Silence retirement | With at least 64 abandoned IDs, retire after one existing 30-second deadline window without an inbound frame, measured from the later of the earliest remaining expiry/interruption and newest frame. The reason names the abandoned count and silence duration. |\n| Inbound liveness | Pushes, uncorrelated responses and late replies count; a single-attachment header counts before its body completes. Activity postpones retirement for the full window. |\n| Late replies | Consume the late response and free its ID exactly once. An abandoned reservation retains correlation only, without the request payload or response body. |\n| Terminal events | Genuine transport failure and explicit close still settle pending callers. The first selected result wins; active callers settled by silence retirement receive its reason. |\n\nAdmission refusal returns `ResponseUnavailable`, `INTERNAL_ERROR`, and a local `RESPONSE_READ` marker with the actual outstanding count. It leaves the healthy full stream open and avoids automatic replay/replacement. The silence timer carries only a weak stream reference and generation; schedule/unschedule, physical socket I/O and callbacks run outside the correlation lock. The original deadline timestamp survives delayed caller cleanup.\n\nIndependent F1 review found one additional cleanup bug: after a body was abandoned while a public read was in flight, owner close or release could interrupt the protocol reader before its drain cleanup began. The body kept its correct closed error, but its forwarding lease remained held. Two real-socket public-API reproducers cover close and `releaseAfterForwarding`; the close case fails 10/10 F1 runs at https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/commit/c801ba96129cab9c69261b4b512e94b4219f86c6 with `Expected <0>, actual <1>` active transfer. The fix preserves the selected body result while completing terminal discard cleanup, including watchdog/input/lease release and existing outer-writer ownership.\n\nReview adds deterministic ManualClock coverage for inbound frames at +29/+31 seconds and for an actual timer reschedule overlapping another abandonment and owner close before both new handles return. Both timer controls pass unchanged F1, so the review found no reason to alter the timer implementation. Admission controls now assert exact local phase/data, and the corrected original close fixture also checks that forwarding storage returns to zero. No timeout or iteration bound changed; no test was disabled, skipped or removed.\n\nLocal verification of https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/commit/eba7f8e6bd763e61e0be20ca605c5ab013c33ea9: normal whole-source build PASS; **49/49** targeted TCP/forwarded/owned scenarios PASS with testParallelism=1; **10/10 fresh JVMs each** for terminal close, terminal release and the corrected original controlled fixture (30/30). The corrected original fixture also passed 10/10 unchanged-F1 runs before the review fix. The 49 canonical test bodies were compared against the branch and differ only in the dependency rule pointing to this lane's immutable normal Maven output. No source-file overlays were used. Product source tree: `2dced01970fd405d8610d635c28bccd547df6a90`; jar SHA-256: `eaa406356dab08a110635044f7818246719ec6f2b4a59987040c2605c0d4d41e`. These are targeted local results; final full-suite/required CI is still a landing gate.\n\nThe earlier Actions failures and their original attribution are recorded at https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/actions/runs/38613501283/job/116022575727 and in the prior evidence: https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/PlanRepository/tree/evidence/lane92-bounded-silent-peer-20261014/handoffs/artifacts/2026-10-14-lane92. Independent review evidence, complete failure stacks, driver provenance and final results: https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/PlanRepository/tree/evidence/lane100-f1-independent-review-20261014/handoffs/artifacts/2026-10-14-lane100.\n\nFinal required CI remains a landing gate. No merge, enqueue, artifact publication or deployment was performed by this lane.\n\nRebased onto main after [PR 693](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/693) and [PR 695](https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/695) merged (the sole conflict was `build.kts`; coordinate `0.0.1403` was retained). All 45 required tests ran serially: 37/37 passed in lane 120, 8/8 passed in lane 127, for 45 passed and 0 failed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-14T16:14:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T01:28:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"475ac9e4a5bfb56202cda7138662b05b37c185ec","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pulls/702/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pulls/702/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/issues/702/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/statuses/527cdb1fbd80ce5e2eee3cc858dc5